{"id": 46, "ts": 1781196570.672881, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I agree with Sarah and Emily that Candidate\u202fB is the stronger overall choice. While Candidate\u202fC offers impressive reliability, rapid correct decisions and calmness in crises, we have no evidence of his technical or cognitive competence\u2014no indication that he can understand complex aircraft systems or handle demanding operational tasks. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB demonstrably \u201cassesses weather conditions\u201d and has \u201cexcellent computer skills,\u201d both clear markers of the analytical and systems\u2011oriented abilities essential for long\u2011distance flights. His \u201cvery conscientious\u201d nature satisfies operational reliability, and he \u201chandles stress very well,\u201d covering stress resilience. The concerns about his \u201cnasty remarks\u201d and a \u201cweak memory for numbers\u201d are real but are specific, observable issues that can be addressed through training and monitoring, whereas the absence of any technical competence for C is a fundamental gap. Therefore, I shift my vote to Candidate\u202fB as the best fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
